### What version of the Codex App are you using?

Observed on 2026-10-10:
- Windows Store package: OpenAI.Codex 26.1007.2314.0, SignatureKind Store, Status Ok.
- In-app update checker: release 26.1007.21434, build 13901, prod, up_to_date.
- Computer Use plugin: 26.1007.21434; bundled @oai/sky: 0.7.6.
These are separately obtained package/release identifiers, not a claim of version corruption.

### What subscription do you have?

Omitted from this sanitized report. Please triage the technical reproduction without account information.

### What platform is your computer?

Windows 10.0.26300.0, x64. Standalone .NET Framework WinForms fixture; documented sky APIs through the persistent Node REPL.

### What issue are you seeing?

A freshly captured parent-window accessibility tree exposes an editable owned-dialog field, but indexed set_value against that parent Window fails. Resolving the actual owned-dialog Window from list_windows, recapturing it, and setting the same field with its fresh index succeeds.

| Operation | Observed result |
|---|---|
| Main-window MainValue set_value | Success; MAIN_SET_VALUE_OK |
| Owned DialogValue exposed in fresh parent snapshot (index 13 in this run), set_value targeting parent | `element 13 is not available in cached app state for NativeInputFixture.exe`; value unchanged |
| Same DialogValue via actual dialog Window returned by list_windows and its own fresh index (1 in this run) | Success; MODAL_DIRECT_OK |
| Classic SaveFileDialog filename advertised as settable/string in fresh parent snapshot (index 70 in this run) | `Cannot set a value for an element that is not settable`; filename unchanged |

The classic SaveFileDialog was not independently returned by list_windows, so the successful owned-Form retargeting path was unavailable for it. Indices above are observations, not values to hard-code.

The user confirmed pausing keyboard and mouse input during this dedicated test. The fixture recorded only its own messages/control events, without global hooks or input injection. It recorded exactly the two expected text changes above. Save As was cancelled, the fixture was closed, and no user document was used.

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

1. Compile the self-contained source below in a disposable writable directory. From a Developer Command Prompt with .NET Framework csc available:

```text
csc /nologo /target:winexe /out:NativeInputFixture.exe /reference:System.Windows.Forms.dll /reference:System.Drawing.dll /reference:System.Web.Extensions.dll NativeInputFixture.cs
```

2. Launch through documented sky.launch_app with the fixture's local executable path. Resolve its main Window from list_windows. Request get_window_state with both include_screenshot and include_text true.
3. Set MainValue through its freshly observed index. This succeeds.
4. Open OpenOwnedDialog. Capture the parent Window again. Find DialogValue in that returned tree and call set_value using the parent Window and that fresh index. Observe the cached-app-state error with the field unchanged.
5. Obtain the owned dialog's actual Window from list_windows, capture its own state, and call set_value with its own fresh DialogValue index. This succeeds. Close the dialog.
6. Capture the main window including a screenshot and open OpenClassicSaveAs. Capture again. The filename is advertised editable/settable, but set_value fails as above. The classic modal is absent from list_windows. Cancel and close the fixture.

An indexed click after a text-only capture also returned `coordinate input geometry is unavailable`; including a fresh screenshot allowed that click. This is recorded separately, not established as the cause of either set_value failure.

### What is the expected behavior?

Editable elements advertised in a returned snapshot should resolve consistently for that snapshot/window. The active modal should be exposed as a supported target when required. ValuePattern operations should have the UIA properties they need cached, or return an actionable unsupported-control explanation before attempting input.

### Requested Windows native diagnosis and official fix

Please route this deterministic standalone reproduction to the Windows Computer Use/native maintainers and investigate:

1. Parent/owned-modal window selection and cache namespace/generation used by observation versus indexed input.
2. UIA CacheRequest coverage for ValuePattern and read-only/settable property checks.
3. Activation/focus before dispatch and any delayed/cross-request input delivery. An earlier unexpected-text observation remains unexplained; no unintended text was reproduced in this instrumented trial, so this report does not claim the cache error caused it.
4. Provide a supported diagnostic build or minimal privacy-preserving tracing instructions, and deliver an official signed update when a fix is verified. Local source/mock candidates have not been installed into the Store package or native runtime.

A separate source-level review found shared-helper lifecycle/approval races; a local candidate passed 44 mocked regression cases, but neither its relationship to the cache/input symptom nor native integration is established. Extracted proprietary source and candidate code are deliberately not published here. Please advise a supported engineering handoff if useful.

Related observations: #42899 and #43101. This report adds a standalone fixture and a same-field comparison between parent targeting and a dialog Window actually returned by list_windows; it does not assert those reports have the same internal cause.

### Privacy and evidence boundary

This submission contains only the sanitized reproduction and self-authored fixture source. No raw logs, session/conversation IDs, account/subscription identifiers, personal local paths, screenshots, user documents, native binaries, or extracted application source are included. The fixture can generate local diagnostics when maintainers run it, but no generated event log is submitted. A mock pass is not a native or production repair claim.

<details>
<summary>Self-contained NativeInputFixture.cs</summary>

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;
using System.Drawing;
using System.Windows.Forms;
using System.Web.Script.Serialization;

// Diagnostic application only. No input injection, global hooks, network, or shell commands.
static class TraceLog {
    public static readonly string Root=AppDomain.CurrentDomain.BaseDirectory;
    public static readonly string PathName=Path.Combine(Root,"native-input-fixture-events.jsonl");
    public static void Write(string kind, object data) {
        File.AppendAllText(PathName,new JavaScriptSerializer().Serialize(new {utc=DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("o"),kind=kind,data=data})+"\n",new UTF8Encoding(false));
    }
    public static void Attach(Control c) {
        c.GotFocus+=(s,e)=>Write("focus",new {control=c.Name,handle=c.Handle.ToInt64()});
        c.KeyDown+=(s,e)=>Write("keydown",new {control=c.Name,key=e.KeyData.ToString()});
        c.KeyPress+=(s,e)=>Write("keypress",new {control=c.Name,code=(int)e.KeyChar});
        c.MouseDown+=(s,e)=>Write("mousedown",new {control=c.Name,x=e.X,y=e.Y,button=e.Button.ToString()});
        if(c is TextBox)c.TextChanged+=(s,e)=>Write("text",new {control=c.Name,value=c.Text});
    }
}
sealed class OwnMessageTrace:IMessageFilter {
    public bool PreFilterMessage(ref Message m) {
        if(m.Msg==0x100 || m.Msg==0x101 || m.Msg==0x102 || m.Msg==0x201 || m.Msg==0x202)
            TraceLog.Write("thread-message",new {handle=m.HWnd.ToInt64(),message=m.Msg,wparam=m.WParam.ToInt64(),lparam=m.LParam.ToInt64()});
        return false;
    }
}
sealed class FixtureForm:Form {
    readonly TextBox main=new TextBox();
    public FixtureForm() {
        Text="Computer Use Input Diagnostic Fixture";Name="DiagnosticMain";ClientSize=new Size(720,300);StartPosition=FormStartPosition.CenterScreen;
        var label=new Label {Text="Main value (diagnostic text only)",Left=25,Top=25,Width=650};
        main.Name="MainValue";main.AccessibleName="MainValue";main.SetBounds(25,55,650,35);main.Text="MAIN_BASELINE";
        var modal=new Button {Name="OpenOwnedDialog",Text="Open owned dialog",Left=25,Top=120,Width=200,Height=40};
        var save=new Button {Name="OpenClassicSaveAs",Text="Open classic Save As",Left=250,Top=120,Width=220,Height=40};
        var close=new Button {Name="CloseFixture",Text="Close fixture",Left=495,Top=120,Width=180,Height=40};
        modal.Click+=(s,e)=>{
            TraceLog.Write("modal-open",new {main=main.Text});
            using(var d=new Form {Name="DiagnosticOwned",Text="Diagnostic owned dialog",ClientSize=new Size(500,180),StartPosition=FormStartPosition.CenterParent}) {
                var field=new TextBox {Name="DialogValue",AccessibleName="DialogValue",Text="MODAL_BASELINE",Left=25,Top=35,Width=440};
                var done=new Button {Name="CloseModal",Text="Close modal",Left=300,Top=105,Width=160,Height=35};
                done.Click+=(a,b)=>d.Close();d.Controls.Add(field);d.Controls.Add(done);
                TraceLog.Attach(field);TraceLog.Attach(done);d.Shown+=(a,b)=>{field.Focus();field.SelectAll();TraceLog.Write("modal-shown",new {handle=d.Handle.ToInt64(),fieldHandle=field.Handle.ToInt64()});};
                d.ShowDialog(this);TraceLog.Write("modal-closed",new {main=main.Text,value=field.Text});
            }
        };
        save.Click+=(s,e)=>{
            TraceLog.Write("save-open",new {main=main.Text});
            using(var d=new SaveFileDialog {AutoUpgradeEnabled=false,InitialDirectory=TraceLog.Root,FileName="fixture-probe.txt",Filter="Text files (*.txt)|*.txt",AddExtension=true,OverwritePrompt=true}) {
                d.FileOk+=(a,b)=>{string target=Path.GetFullPath(d.FileName);if(!target.StartsWith(TraceLog.Root,StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)){b.Cancel=true;TraceLog.Write("save-outside-root-blocked",new {});}};
                var result=d.ShowDialog(this);TraceLog.Write("save-result",new {result=result.ToString(),filename=d.FileName,main=main.Text});
                if(result==DialogResult.OK)File.WriteAllText(d.FileName,main.Text,new UTF8Encoding(false));
            }
        };
        close.Click+=(s,e)=>Close();
        Controls.AddRange(new Control[]{label,main,modal,save,close});
        foreach(Control c in Controls)TraceLog.Attach(c);
        Shown+=(s,e)=>{main.Focus();main.SelectAll();TraceLog.Write("main-shown",new {handle=Handle.ToInt64(),mainHandle=main.Handle.ToInt64(),main=main.Text});};
        FormClosed+=(s,e)=>TraceLog.Write("app-closed",new {main=main.Text});
    }
    protected override void WndProc(ref Message m) {
        if(m.Msg==0x6 || m.Msg==0x7 || m.Msg==0x8)TraceLog.Write("main-window-message",new {handle=m.HWnd.ToInt64(),message=m.Msg,wparam=m.WParam.ToInt64(),lparam=m.LParam.ToInt64()});
        base.WndProc(ref m);
    }
    [STAThread] static void Main() {
        TraceLog.Write("app-start",new {process=System.Diagnostics.Process.GetCurrentProcess().Id});
        Application.EnableVisualStyles();Application.SetCompatibleTextRenderingDefault(false);
        Application.AddMessageFilter(new OwnMessageTrace());Application.Run(new FixtureForm());
    }
}

```

</details>

## What issue are you seeing?

The comment above `sanitize_responses_api_tool_name` says that characters disallowed by the Responses API are replaced with `_`, and cites the pattern `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$`.

However, the implementation also replaces `-` with `_`, even though hyphens are allowed by that pattern:

```rust
if c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || c == '_' {
    sanitized.push(c);
} else {
    sanitized.push('_');
}
```

Source: [codex-rs/codex-mcp/src/mcp/mod.rs](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/codex-mcp/src/mcp/mod.rs#L579-L598)

I initially read this as an inconsistency between the comment and implementation.

## Additional context

This appears to be intentional: [PR #14605](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/14605) changed the sanitizer to replace hyphens for Code Mode compatibility, so function names and Code Mode names use the same format. [PR #16944](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/16944) also mentions this constraint.

## Suggested improvement

Could the comment mention the stricter Code Mode naming requirement in addition to the Responses API pattern? That would make the reason for replacing `-` clear when reading the function.

No behavior change is needed.
